Input/output redirection
echo "Hello Linux" > file.txt


Creates a file and writes content into it.
echo "Welcome" >> file.txt


Appends content to the file.
cat < file.txt


Takes input from a file.
ls > output.txt


Redirects output into a file.
ls nonexistent 2> error.txt


Redirects error messages into a file.
C. Pipe commands
A pipe (|) sends the output of one command to another command.
ls | wc -l


Counts the number of listed entries.
cat file.txt | sort


Sorts the contents of a file.
ps aux | grep bash


Searches for Bash processes.
